n{{field-1}}" 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186162529 1074 "The supremum of a set $A$ is the smallest upper bound of $A.$\n\nIf $A$ is a finite set, the supremum of $A$ equals its maximum. \n\nFirst, let's write down all the terms of our set by substituting $n=1,2,3,4$ into the expression for the elements of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(-1)^{1}}{(1)^{2}+1} & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{(-1)^{2}}{(2)^{2}+1} & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\frac{(-1)^{3}}{(3)^{2}+1} & =-\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ \\frac{(-1)^{4}}{(4)^{2}+1} & =\\frac{1}{17}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nA=\\{-\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{1}{5},\\,-\\frac{1}{10},\\,\\frac{1}{17}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sup(A) & =max\\{-\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{1}{5},\\,-\\frac{1}{10},\\,\\frac{1}{17}\\}=\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186166825 1038 #edb/ref 17592186489202 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186166825 1038 #edb/ref 17592186489223 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186166825 1038 #edb/ref 17592186489270 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186166825 1038 #edb/ref 17592186489271 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186166826 1038 #edb/ref 17592186489191 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186166826 1038 #edb/ref 17592186489210 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186166826 1038 #edb/ref 17592186489272 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186166826 1038 #edb/ref 17592186489273 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186166831 1038 #edb/ref 17592186489190 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186166831 1038 #edb/ref 17592186489215 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186166831 1038 #edb/ref 17592186489251 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186166831 1038 #edb/ref 17592186489278 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186166998 1050 540.0 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186176091 1038 #edb/ref 17592186489296 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186176092 1038 #edb/ref 1