f8b8f453-e893-54c0-b002-e0291533bd6d" 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489380 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489209 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489381 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489368 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489381 1062 #uuid "f954900d-db8e-5669-983f-61ddeb5299ad" 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489381 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489220 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489382 1062 #uuid "fa750b8a-5567-556e-812e-8c8f5c7c8f4e" 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489382 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489232 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489383 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489366 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489383 1062 #uuid "fc7884c4-a77b-566a-b6c8-506309c43c66" 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489383 1063 #edb/ref 17592186427561 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489384 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489350 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489384 1062 #uuid "fdc1b998-1ffd-53d7-9edb-119354e86ad0" 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489384 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125186 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489385 1064 "A rational number can have a decimal representation that either *ends* or *repeats*.\n\nIn this lesson, we will see how to convert rational numbers written as fractions into decimals using *long division*. \nWe begin with examples where the decimal terminates. \n\nLet's convert $\\dfrac{7}{2}$ into a decimal using long division.\n\nTo write the fraction as a decimal, we divide the numerator by the denominator:\n\n$$\n7 \\div 2\n$$\n\nWe proceed using long division as usual, stopping once we obtain a remainder of $0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"2\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,3    {\\, . \\,} 5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"2\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\!\\require{enclose}\\enclose{longdiv}{7   {\\, . \\,} 0}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{7}{2} = 3.5.\n$$" 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489385 1065 15179 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489385 1066 #uuid "6c539020-aca7-5b8f-a2b0-b72c56336242" 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489385 1067 "Introduction" 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489386 1064 "The key takeaway for this lesson is that every repeating decimal is rational! In other words, every repeating decimal can be expressed as a ratio of two integers.\n\nFor example:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.\\overset{―}{3} & =\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0.\\overset{―}{78} & =\\frac{26}{33} \\\\ 0.333\\overset{―}{67} & =\\frac{16517}{49500}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn a future lesson, we'll learn how to express a repeating decimal as a fraction. For now, you can verify these results using a calculator." 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489386 1065 15181 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489386 1066 #uuid "77b1162b-17a9-5251-8efe-31b7034274d5" 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489386 1067 "Any Repeating Decimal is a Rational" 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489387 1064 "It's convenient to use the following special **bar-notation** to indicate decimals that repeat indefinitely:\n\n$$\n0.\\overline{3} = 0.333\\,333\\ldots\n$$\n\nSome decimals have two or more digits that repeat indefinitely. For example:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.\\overset{―}{78} & =0.78\\,78\\,78\\,78… \\\\ 0.\\overset{―}{675} & =0.675\\,675\\,675…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSome repeating decimals have non-repeating digits before the repeating part. For example:\n\n$$\n0.45\\overline{67} = 0.45\\,67\\,67\\,67\\,67\\ldots\n$$" 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489387 1065 15180 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489387 1066 #uuid "8545445f-23ee-5309-8571-5a1f6a4b253d" 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489387 1067 "Notations for Repeating Decimals" 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489388 1064 "Let's consider the following rational number:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac13\n$$\n\nTo find its decimal representation, we divide $1$ by $3$ using long division, as follows:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"4\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,0 \\,. 3 {\\:\\phantom{|}} 3 {\\:\\phantom{|}} 3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\:\\ldots$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$3$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"4\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\!\\require{enclose}\\enclose{longdiv}{1 {\\, . \\,} 0  {\\:\\phantom{|}} 0 {\\:\\phantom{|}} 0}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$9$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$9$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$9$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\ldots$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNotice that, in this case,\n\n- the long division process never ends, and\n\n- the digit $3$ after the decimal point repeats *forever*.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac13 = 0.333\\,333\\ldots\n$$\n\nThis is an example of a **repeating decimal** - a decimal in which the digits after the decimal point continue forever in a *repeating pattern*." 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489388 1065 15177 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489388 1066 #uuid "b877953a-1821-5fae-aebf-3ff936971679" 13194139535272 17592186045417 true] [17592186489388 1067 "Repeating Decimals" 13194139535272 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-00a00fae-87cf-57ec-8a60-95f73cd3d46c" 17592186488449 "activity-05594f5b-c67a-5e94-adc0-9f23070bfc99" 17592186488450 "activity-06eed5f8-017a-533b-a592-9dd0d3097b53" 17592186488451 "activity-338c1f36-4052-519c-8f01-5e5af20b10f1" 17592186488452 "activity-371228db-c3aa-592c-9027-4958f292ca14" 17592186488453 "activity-4dc0b406-c0b6-53ca-9886-dcf9b9543412" 17592186488454 "activity-5d7d6b48-4082-54df-a38c-264067bb8314" 17592186488455 "activity-60936641-355a-54ca-910d-83aee7c18376" 17592186488456 "activity-703238ea-d56c-59ca-8e67-df48e350b9bb" 17592186488457 "activity-8832ccc5-5062-53eb-9aa3-cff46feb853b" 17592186488458 "activity-a131be7b-68d2-57db-b50e-5c3bbbbafaae" 17592186488459 "activity-a3308d93-fc2c-5afd-b2a2-d10eabcc55b8" 17592186488460 "activity-a5e50e5c-f6d4-570d-8bfd-dd50d0a5e6dd" 17592186488461 "activity-c50fc124-2e70-50d8-bf4f-018c42fcb65d" 17592186488462 "activity-c74fe8fe-ab17-5021-aa6e-cba45f79c1ff" 17592186488463 "activity-e818d606-33e5-5229-a600-ada8b5ddee18" 17592186488464 "activity-e9225a93-dc03-57da-bec9-4f535a279d72" 17592186488465 "activity-f5d315b3-1937-5219-9b02-93324c4b74bb" 17592186488466 "activity-fd6c1f5e-0479-589e-8277-39b3bde8383f" 17592186488467 "answer-0118c6ec-baa3-5b9a-b5f